WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.318
Extracting astrophysics from gravitational waves
needs Bayesian inference,

00:00:05.398 --> 00:00:07.361
and that needs a likelihood.

00:00:07.441 --> 00:00:14.729
For decades the field assumed noise is Gaussian and
stationary because it makes the likelihood cheap.

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:21.513
But real detectors drift over time and carry
transient glitches and wandering spectral lines.

00:00:21.593 --> 00:00:27.641
These are handled segment by segment with costly
custom fixes that can bias results.

00:00:27.721 --> 00:00:31.580
Famously, GW170817 landed right on a loud LIGO glitch.
